{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>To Moses in Midian.</b> The verse's intention in informing us that the speech was in Midian is to declare the praise of Moses, that he paid no mind to his enemies who were in Egypt at the time he pressed his many arguments, for in all his arguments he was concerned only on account of the weakening of the power of the mission, not out of personal fear. The proof that he did not argue because he was afraid of those seeking his life is this: had the verse not said 'in Midian,' the logical assumption would be that Moses had not firmly decided in his mind to go on the mission until he was assured from the mouth of El that those seeking his life had died. Therefore it says <b>in Midian</b>, to say that only after he had firmly decided and agreed with HaShem to go was he informed of this — and this matter had not been holding him back."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:24:33.555168511Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}